From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT=<MiB>: with the pool short and the images under the collector's 1024 MiB floor, clean idle images still go (32 a frame, unused 120 frames); off by default

Switches: EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT=<MiB> (1 to 65535, digits only; unset, 0 or anything else: off).
EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT_AGE=<frames> (unset, 0 or not a number: 120; at least 10). Line (log
macro, HW.GPU, eden_log): "EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT 600 frames: ..." when the case came up.

Why (READ, a hand-played session and a hand-played session, T151, the load
into the area past the field): TextureCache::TickFrame calls RunGarbageCollector only while
total_used_memory > minimum_memory, and minimum_memory is 1024 MiB on the console ("Texture cache
thresholds: expected 2560 MiB, critical 3328 MiB, minimum 1024 MiB"). The Vulkan port's pool signal
(PoolPressure: largest free block under 256 MiB = aggressive) lives inside RunGarbageCollector, so
with the images under 1024 MiB nothing reads it. On the console the guest (5.7-6.3 GB), the heap
(1.5-2.0 GB) and the JIT (0.5 GB) leave the pool empty while the images are under that floor:
- handheld: EDEN_MEM_CENSUS n=37..50, largest free block 0-192 MiB, images 932-1013 MiB, at n=42
  664 MiB of them unused for 120 frames and clean; not one deleted until the load (images=964/968
  for 16 s). The load then needed +2.2 GB of graphics memory in 7 s and the session died at 0 MiB.
- docked: n=265..296 (two minutes), largest 0-182 MiB, images 925-1019 MiB, 592 MiB clean stale.
What: ShortPoolCollect(), at the end of the frame after AreaEvict and before the collector. The
pool's largest free block (MemoryCensus::FreeLargest, the front's kernel query the census thread
makes every 250 ms) is read every 30 frames. While it is under <MiB> and the collector is
skipped (images <= minimum_memory), up to 32 images a frame that have not been used for the age
go, oldest first: only what AreaEvict would delete too (no copy back, no staging, no GPU wait),
less the costly ones (CostlyLoad, CPU-decoded, decoding, kept as re-made). A deleted image is
uploaded again from guest memory if the game uses it again. Above the floor the collector runs as
before and this does nothing. Off: one test of a static per frame. Where FreeLargest is 0 (no
front figure) it does nothing.
Expected (log replay, t155/check/host/replay.log): with 1024 it acts at 20 of 57 handheld censuses
(n=37..50 with up to 664 MiB to delete) and 42 of 339 docked ones (n=265..296, up to 592 MiB).
Risk: textures unused for 2 s (120 frames) that come back into view are uploaded again (a frame
or a few of a late texture). Not on the console yet.
Timing correction (checker, our notes, put in at T160): the clean
stale part was 0-134 MiB through the field (handheld n=21-41, docked n=260-268) and rose to 664 / 592
MiB only at n=42 / n=270, the start of the area change, not "for 1-2 minutes". This pass therefore
has a window of about 10 s handheld and 5-8 s docked before the load's long frame, while frames
still tick; the window is not guaranteed. The code comment says the same since T160.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index be3aad7673..fdffc7d88f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -1169,6 +1169,121 @@ void TextureCache<P>::CensusTick() {
     MemoryCensus::ImagesPublished(request);
 }
 
+// EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT=<MiB> (1 to 65535, digits only; unset, 0 or anything else: off, as
+// before). The collector runs only while the images add up to more than minimum_memory (1024 MiB
+// on the console), and its own pool signal (the Vulkan port's PoolPressure) lives inside it. On
+// the console the guest, the heap and the JIT take 8 to 8.5 GB of the 12.3 GB pool, so the pool
+// can be empty with the images under that floor, and then nothing is collected at all. Ocarina
+// of Time, the field before the load into the area past it (crash-20261113-064906 handheld,
+// crash-20261113-063844 docked): the largest free block under 200 MiB, the images at about 930 to
+// 1020 MiB. Through the field only 0 to 134 MiB of them were clean and unused for 120 frames
+// (EDEN_MEM_CENSUS n=21 to 41 handheld, n=260 to 268 docked); that jumped to 664 MiB (n=42) and
+// 592 MiB (n=270) only when the area change began. So this pass has a window of about 10 s
+// handheld and 5 to 8 s docked before the load's long frame, and only while frames keep ticking
+// (it runs in TickFrame); a faster load gives a shorter window. The load then asked for 2.2 GB of
+// graphics memory in 7 s and the session died with 0 MiB free.
+// With the switch: the pool's largest free block (MemoryCensus::FreeLargest, the census thread's
+// kernel query) is read every 30 frames; while it is under <MiB> and the collector is skipped,
+// images unused for EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT_AGE frames (unset: 120, at least 10) go at the end of
+// the frame, 32 a frame, oldest first. Only images AreaEvict would also delete, less the costly
+// ones: nothing the GPU wrote (no copy back, no staging, no wait), nothing decoding or decoded on
+// the CPU (the 1365x1365x90 arrays take 4.5 s each), nothing the collector keeps as re-made, no
+// CostlyLoad image. A deleted image is uploaded again from guest memory if it is used again.
+// Line: "EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT 600 frames: ..." when anything was short in the last 600 frames.
+// When the images pass the floor, the collector itself runs (with PoolPressure) and this does
+// nothing. Where the front has no pool figure (FreeLargest 0) it does nothing either.
+[[nodiscard]] inline u64 ShortCollectBytes() {
+    static const u64 bytes = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT");
+        if (value == nullptr || value[0] == '\0') {
+            return u64{0};
+        }
+        u64 mib = 0;
+        for (const char* digit = value; *digit != '\0'; ++digit) {
+            if (*digit < '0' || *digit > '9') {
+                return u64{0};
+            }
+            mib = mib * 10 + static_cast<u64>(*digit - '0');
+            if (mib > 65535) {
+                return u64{0};
+            }
+        }
+        return mib << 20;
+    }();
+    return bytes;
+}
+
+[[nodiscard]] inline u64 ShortCollectAge() {
+    static const u64 frames = [] {
+        const char* const value = std::getenv("EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT_AGE");
+        const u64 age = value != nullptr ? std::strtoull(value, nullptr, 10) : 0ULL;
+        return age == 0 ? u64{120} : (std::max)(age, u64{10}); // unset, 0 or not a number: 120
+    }();
+    return frames;
+}
+
+template <class P>
+void TextureCache<P>::ShortPoolCollect() {
+    const u64 limit = ShortCollectBytes();
+    if (limit == 0) {
+        return;
+    }
+    constexpr u64 SampleFrames = 30;
+    constexpr u64 LogFrames = 600;
+    constexpr size_t MaxPerFrame = 32;
+    if (short_collect_sample_frame == 0 || frame_tick - short_collect_sample_frame >= SampleFrames) {
+        short_collect_sample_frame = frame_tick != 0 ? frame_tick : 1;
+        short_collect_largest = MemoryCensus::FreeLargest();
+        short_collect_short = short_collect_largest != 0 && short_collect_largest < limit;
+    }
+    if (frame_tick - short_collect_logged >= LogFrames) {
+        if (short_collect_frames != 0) {
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                     "EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT {} frames: {} frames with the pool under {} MiB and "
+                     "the images under the collector's {} MiB floor; {} images, {} MiB deleted "
+                     "(unused for {} frames, clean); now: largest free block {} MiB, images {} MiB",
+                     frame_tick - short_collect_logged, short_collect_frames, limit >> 20,
+                     minimum_memory >> 20, short_collect_images, short_collect_bytes >> 20,
+                     ShortCollectAge(), short_collect_largest >> 20, total_used_memory >> 20);
+        }
+        short_collect_logged = frame_tick;
+        short_collect_frames = short_collect_images = short_collect_bytes = 0;
+    }
+    if (!short_collect_short || total_used_memory > minimum_memory) {
+        return; // not short, or the collector runs this frame anyway
+    }
+    ++short_collect_frames;
+    const u64 age = ShortCollectAge();
+    if (frame_tick <= age) {
+        return;
+    }
+    boost::container::small_vector<ImageId, MaxPerFrame> doomed;
+    u64 bytes = 0;
+    lru_cache.ForEachItemBelow(frame_tick - age, [&](ImageId image_id) {
+        const Image& image = slot_images[image_id];
+        if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::IsDecoding) ||
+            True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::AsynchronousDecode) ||
+            True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::CostlyLoad) || KeptRemade(image) ||
+            (IsDownloadable(image) && False(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::BadOverlap))) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        bytes += ImageMemoryBytes(image) + (image.HasScaled() ? GetScaledImageSizeBytes(image) : 0);
+        doomed.push_back(image_id);
+        return doomed.size() == MaxPerFrame;
+    });
+    for (const ImageId image_id : doomed) {
+        Image& image = slot_images[image_id];
+        if (True(image.flags & ImageFlagBits::Tracked)) {
+            UntrackImage(image, image_id);
+        }
+        UnregisterImage(image_id);
+        trace_delete_reason = "short-pool";
+        DeleteImage(image_id, image.scale_tick > frame_tick + 5);
+    }
+    short_collect_images += doomed.size();
+    short_collect_bytes += bytes;
+}
+
 // EDEN_NX2_AREA_EVICT=<frames> (unset or 0: off, as before): when the game changes area, the
 // images of the area it left go before the pool runs dry. The collector keys on its marks and
 // on the pool's largest free block, and on the PS5 both can sit quiet until the pool is gone:
@@ -2234,6 +2349,7 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
     RetireStaleTargets();
     DeleteSupersededImages(); // EDEN_NX2_TC_SUPERSEDED
     AreaEvict();
+    ShortPoolCollect();
     if (total_used_memory > minimum_memory) {
         HitchTrace::Op collector_trace{HitchTrace::Kind::Collector, total_used_memory, {}};
         RunGarbageCollector();
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index ec8dd62031..b218cbbdbd 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -339,6 +339,15 @@ class TextureCache : public VideoCommon::ChannelSetupCaches<TextureCacheChannelI
     u64 census_window_frame{};
     u64 census_window_created{};
     u64 census_quiet_until{}; ///< One area note per load: none again before this frame
+    /// EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT (ShortPoolCollect): the last sample of the pool and the counts
+    /// for its 600-frame line.
+    u64 short_collect_sample_frame{};
+    u64 short_collect_largest{};
+    bool short_collect_short{};
+    u64 short_collect_frames{};  ///< Frames short with the collector skipped (under its floor)
+    u64 short_collect_images{};  ///< Images it deleted
+    u64 short_collect_bytes{};   ///< What they held
+    u64 short_collect_logged{};  ///< frame_tick of the last line
     /// EDEN_NX2_CLEAN_BY_TIME / EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT: when each frame ended (TickFrame).
     FrameClock frame_clock;
     /// EDEN_NX2_REFUSAL_EVICT: allocator refusals already answered at a frame's end.
@@ -512,6 +521,13 @@ public:
     /// of a frame, with mutex held, before the collector.
     void AreaEvict();
 
+    /// EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT=<MiB>: while the pool's largest free block is under <MiB> and the
+    /// images add up to no more than minimum_memory (so the collector does not run), deletes
+    /// images unused for EDEN_UP_TC_SHORT_COLLECT_AGE frames (120) that need no copy back and
+    /// are cheap to make again, 32 a frame. At the end of a frame, with mutex held, before the
+    /// collector. Off: one test of a static.
+    void ShortPoolCollect();
+
     /// EDEN_UP_MEM_CENSUS=1 (video_core/memory_census.h): starts the census thread, tells it when an
     /// area load begins, and when a census asks, hands it what the images hold by kind. At the end
     /// of a frame, with mutex held, before the relocation sweep and AreaEvict.
